.TH TONESTACK-REAPER-SETUP 1 "2026-01-01" "tonestack-plugins" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tonestack-reaper-setup \- add /usr/lib/vst3 to the VST search paths of REAPER
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tonestack-reaper-setup
.RB [ \-\-undo ]
.RB [ \-\-ini
.IR file ]
.br
.B tonestack-reaper-setup
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
REAPER for Linux looks for VST plug-ins only in
.I ~/.vst
and
.I ~/.vst3
by default, so it does not see the VST3 versions of the tonestack plug-ins in
.IR /usr/lib/vst3 .
(The CLAP versions in
.I /usr/lib/clap
are found without any setup.)
.B tonestack-reaper-setup
appends
.I /usr/lib/vst3
to the line
.B vstpath=
of the REAPER configuration file and changes nothing else.
.PP
Run it as the user who uses REAPER, not as root, and only while REAPER is not
running: REAPER writes its configuration back when it exits and would undo the
change. Before the first change the file is copied to
.IR reaper.ini.vor-tonestack ;
the permissions of the file are kept. The file
.I reaper.ini.tonestack
next to it records that the entry was added by this program.
.PP
The package tonestack-plugins runs this program for every user who has set up
REAPER when it is installed, with the rights of that user, and takes the entry
out again when the package is removed (only an entry that it added itself, and
only if no other plug-ins are left in
.IR /usr/lib/vst3 ).
.PP
Afterwards, in REAPER: Options > Preferences > Plug-ins > VST > Re-scan.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-undo
Take
.I /usr/lib/vst3
out of the VST search paths again.
.TP
.BI \-\-ini " file"
Use another REAPER configuration file, for example that of a portable
installation. Default:
.IR ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/REAPER/reaper.ini .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help text (in German).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success or when there is nothing to do, 1 on errors, 2 when REAPER is
running and nothing was changed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/REAPER/reaper.ini
REAPER configuration (line
.BR vstpath= ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/REAPER/reaper.ini.vor-tonestack
Copy made before the first change.
.TP
.I ~/.config/REAPER/reaper.ini.tonestack
Marks the entry as added by this program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/tonestack-plugins/README-Linux.txt
.SH AUTHOR
tonestack, https://github.com/colonade/tonestack
